<title>UK: Guinness, GrandMet shares push up.</title>
<headline>Guinness, GrandMet shares push up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Guinness Plc and Grand Metropolitan Plc moved ahead on Wednesday after French luxury goods company LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton announced a plan for merging its drinks business with Guinness and GrandMet.</p>
<p>Guinness shares were up 8-1/2p to 619-1/2p while GrandMet rose 9p to 615-1/2p on the news.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the end of a bit of uncertainty,&quot; said Nick Lyall, an analyst at SocGen.</p>
<p>&quot;This is really what the market expected in the first place - one main spirits company and the demerger of the other businesses to create three separate companies,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
